  <layout>One column of italic verse, set in lines with no stanza breaks. Running head top left, page number top right. No marginal notes and no text below the verse.</layout>
  <page_number>59</page_number>
  <running_head>GVISIACA,</running_head>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1" para="true">
      <i>Non ulla luctu mœsta caret domus,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="2">
      <i>Plorat mariti funera tristior</i>
    </l>
    <l n="3">
      <i>Coniux, &amp; amisso tenellis</i>
    </l>
    <l n="4">
      <i>Patre timet mala plura natis.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="5">
      <i>Maternus, eheu! quæ dolor excitat</i>
    </l>
    <l n="6">
      <i>Lamenta, telis pectora quum videt</i>
    </l>
    <l n="7">
      <i>Traiecta natorum, paterve[?]</i>
    </l>
    <l n="8">
      <i>Quum senior sepelit cruentos!</i>
    </l>
    <l n="9">
      <i>Quæ cuncta Gallis vulnera Gallicus</i>
    </l>
    <l n="10">
      <i>Fecisse miles gestit acerbius,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="11">
      <i>Francosque victos Francus</i>
    </l>
    <l n="12">
      <i>audet Egregius spoliare victor!</i>
    </l>
    <l n="13">
      <i>Antiqua priscis temporibus fides,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="14">
      <i>Virtúsque Francis subdita Regibus,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="15">
      <i>Hostes remotos impetuit</i>
    </l>
    <l n="16">
      <i>Arma ferens metuenda cunctis:</i>
    </l>
    <l n="17">
      <i>Et signa iustis splendida Laureis</i>
    </l>
    <l n="18">
      <i>Late per orbem Gallica protulit,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="19">
      <i>Duxitque laudatos renidens</i>
    </l>
    <l n="20">
      <i>Barbaricis opibus triumphos.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="21">
      <i>Sed nunc benignus te superum favor,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="22">
      <i>Rex magne, nostris fletibus annuit,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="23">
      <i>Plebes ut oppressas benignus</i>
    </l>
    <l n="24">
      <i>Tabifico releues labore</i>
    </l>
    <l n="25">
      <i>Ultor ligato fortior agmine,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="26">
      <i>Gentisque tandem corda recolligas</i>
    </l>
    <l n="27">
      <i>Diuisa, nec posthac redire</i>
    </l>
    <l n="28">
      <i>Indigenas patiare motus.</i>
    </l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Doubtful readings: "paterve" (the last letter, marked [?]); "eheu! quæ" (printed "eheu!qua" with a broken line-end mark). Printed text is set in italic throughout, long s normalised to s, and "Vltor" is written as "Ultor" by the u/v rule.</notes>
</page>
